    "created_at": "2015-12-04T15:34:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-12-04T15:34:43Z",
    "body": "The CanvasRenderingContext2D constructor has to do with CanvasProxy use cases. In a WIP PR I am ripping this out, along with a bunch of other notions that were there just to service CanvasProxy: scratch vs. output bitmaps, setContext() and the notion of unbound contexts, CRC2D being a CanvasImageSource, etc. No one has implemented any of this AFAIK, and it is not need for OffscrenCanvas.\n\nAs for the DrawingStyle thing, I vaguely recall Rik Cabanier making a case for this a few years ago. Other than that, I have not been aware of dev requests for this feature, so it is not in any of our immediate plans to implement this in Blink.  I was sort of expecting Adobe might implement this in all the open source browsers. I guess not. If no one cares enough about this to actually implement it, it might as well go away.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
